    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon matchups, with **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at an elite 82.68. His matchup against Pallante is a primary target; the combination of a high-efficiency park factor and a favorable matchup against a slower-delivery pitcher makes **Corbin Carroll** our highest-upside asset for both power and our scarcest category, SB. Similarly, **James Wood** (78.41) provides a massive spark out of the leadoff spot against a weak pitcher in Lopez. With an elite xwOBA of 0.433 and favorable park conditions, **James Wood** is our secondary anchor. **Isaac Paredes** (70.71) also warrants attention; despite neutral park conditions, his platoon advantage against Young allows him to exceed the 70-point threshold, positioning him as a high-floor play at third base.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was bypassing **Austin Riley** (44.85) in favor of keeping the lineup optimized for efficiency. While **Austin Riley** offers pedigree, his matchup against Eovaldi suppresses his upside, and he ultimately fell behind the aggressive utilization of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte**. Even with **Henry Bolte** slotted in the 8-hole, his total score of 48.01 narrowly outpaces the bench options, and we are betting on his park-adjusted potential in this specific environment. Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** and **Jose Caballero** were strictly excluded as their sub-40 scores fell below our \"Zebras Floor,\" meaning they remain on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more efficient profiles.\n\nManagers should exercise caution regarding **Seiya Suzuki**, who earns a strong 62.44 score but carries a warning for wind blowing in, which could dampen his HR potential. We are also keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing**; his 40.19 score is flirting with our floor, and while his platoon edge against Schlittler is theoretically favorable, the drop-off in output from the #8 spot makes him the most volatile asset in today's starting nine. If the official lineup pushes **Dalton Rushing** or **Henry Bolte** further down the order, we will be forced to reconsider their utility to protect our remaining season-long cap allocation.",
